    "question": "Mrs. Oaklyn buys handmade rugs at $40 each and sells them at $60 each. If she bought 20 rugs, calculate the profit she will make from selling the rugs.",
    "gold": "400",
    "answer": "Since she buys one rug at $40 and sells it at $60, she makes a profit of $60-$40 = $<<60-40=20>>20\nIf she bought 20 rugs at $40 and sold them at $60 each, she made a profit of 20*$20 = $400\n#### 400"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine Mrs. Oaklyn's profit from selling the rugs, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the rugs.\n2. Calculate the total revenue from selling the rugs.\n3. Subtract the total cost from the total revenue to find the profit.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total cost of the rugs.\nMrs. Oaklyn buys each rug for $40 and she bought 20 rugs. Therefore, the total cost is:\n\\[ 40 \\text{ dollars/rug} \\times 20 \\text{ rugs} = 800 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the total revenue from selling the rugs.\nMrs. Oaklyn sells each rug for $60 and she sold 20 rugs. Therefore, the total revenue is:\n\\[ 60 \\text{ dollars/rug} \\times 20 \\text{ rugs} = 1200 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 3: Subtract the total cost from the total revenue to find the profit.\nThe profit is the total revenue minus the total cost:\n\\[ 1200 \\text{ dollars} - 800 \\text{ dollars} = 400 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the profit Mrs. Oaklyn will make from selling the rugs is \\(\\boxed{400}\\).",
